Package: audra
Version: @VERSION@
Architecture: @ARCH@
Maintainer: @MAINTAINER@
Installed-Size: @SIZE@
Section: sound
Priority: optional
Depends: libc6, libgcc-s1, libasound2t64 | libasound2, libwayland-client0, libxkbcommon0, libvulkan1 | libegl1
Recommends: snd-usb-babyface-pro-dkms, pipewire-bin, pulseaudio-utils, xdg-desktop-portal, xdg-utils
Homepage: https://github.com/Vyeche/Audra
Description: hardware mixer for the RME Babyface Pro FS
 Audra controls the onboard DSP mixer of the RME Babyface Pro FS in its
 regular (proprietary) USB mode: routing and submixes, input gain, 48V and
 PAD, EQ and low cut, loopback, and a Control Room with Main, Phones, Dim
 and Talkback. Its layout follows the Windows mixer, TotalMix FX, so people
 coming from it feel at home; it adds snapshots, workspaces, MIDI and Mackie
 Control remote control, and OSC.
 .
 It needs the snd-usb-babyface-pro kernel driver (the
 snd-usb-babyface-pro-dkms package). Based on TuxMix by Ismail Bahloul.
 Not affiliated with or endorsed by RME.
